Push gives observers the data the Subject chooses to send. Pull gives observers access to the Subject and
lets each observer decide what data it needs.

the most important architectural difference
 Push creates stronger coupling around the data contract
 Observer
     ↓
 update(temp, humidity, pressure)

 The observer interface explicitly knows about the data being pushed.

 Pull keeps the notification contract generic
 Observer
     ↓
 update(subject)

 The notification itself is simply:

 "The subject changed."

 The observer determines what to retrieve.

 |                   | Push                                     | Pull                            |
 | ----------------- | ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |
 | Notification      | `update(data)`                           | `update(subject)`               |
 | Who chooses data? | Subject                                  | Observer                        |
 | Subject sends     | Actual data                              | Reference to itself             |
 | Observer          | Receives data                            | Retrieves data                  |
 | Flexibility       | Less flexible as data grows              | More flexible                   |
 | Coupling          | Observer depends on pushed data contract | Observer depends on Subject API |
